	(text "v15-LCD, 2026-10-08. 1.9in 170x320 IPS (ST7789V3) replaces the 2.13in e-paper. Panel = Unvision/Newvisio 190-1732TBWPG01 family (the LilyGO T-Display-S3 / Heltec HT-VMT190 panel), 30-pin 0.5 mm FPC, 4-wire SPI: IM1 = IM2 = VDD, RD and DB0..DB7 to GND (vendor 4-SPI circuit), SDO and TP pins open."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 15 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1a460030-ebec-4369-a9cf-011201853ff9")
	)
	(text "SPI on the old e-paper GPIOs, re-assigned so the board routes without crossings: MOSI IO5, D/C IO6, SCK IO8, CS IO41, RST IO42 (review 13, 2026-10-08: J5 footprint pad numbers are mirrored, pad N = socket contact 31-N, so that panel finger 1 lands on pad 1 after the tail folds through the slot; the five B.Cu lanes keep their order, so the GPIO roles swapped) (any GPIO works through the ESP32-S3 GPIO matrix). IO4 = LCD_BL_EN (PWM; KEYPAD_INT moved from IO4 to IO3, both RTC wake pins). IO33 (was EPD_BUSY) = LCD_PWR_N, active low, R21 pull-up: panel unpowered in deep sleep (ST7789 standby alone is ~20 uA)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 20 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6e83c15e-4843-4825-a2ff-7c30a0f86035")
	)
	(text "Backlight: 4 white LEDs in parallel inside the panel (rated 60 mA, 3.0-3.4 V). LEDA <- R23 15R <- +3V3; the four cathodes are tied (LCD_LEDK) and switched by Q5 (AO3400A) with LEDC PWM on IO4. (3.3 V - Vf ~2.8 V) / 22 R = about 20-25 mA at 100 % duty (~1/3 of rated brightness, enough indoors); R22 keeps Q5 off in deep sleep. A constant-current driver (AW9364, LCSC C401007) is the upgrade if more brightness is wanted."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 25 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "360d35bb-5390-4b8c-a9b1-ee883cfa8dfc")
	)
	(text "Rules: drive every LCD SPI pin low before LCD_PWR_N goes high, or the panel is back-powered through its ESD diodes. BL_EN low in sleep (Q5 off: no backlight current). No TE pin on this panel."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 30 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3ff33578-f157-4fc1-9ec7-6a1bd6346d31")
	)
	(text "Removed vs v14: J2 (24P e-paper socket), the SSD1680 booster L1, Q3, R11, R12, D3, D4, D5, C20..C30 (17 parts). Added: J5, Q4, Q5, R21, R22, R23, C36 (C19 re-used on LCD_VDD)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 33 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "565fdf95-7161-42b9-aaf2-400a8841bf18")
	)
